  "status_text": "Piling on more rules buys no way past 36 pairs. Lean checked the exact ceiling for asking whether any pair of lights is fully on, with four hidden switches and at most six entries per rule. A rulebook exists for every number of pairs up to 36. At 37 pairs or more, every correct rulebook needs a longer clause, however many clauses we allow. The shortest rulebook at the boundary has 88 clauses. Next we ask how the ceiling changes with different hidden-switch and length budgets (L-lib-1152, L-lib-1144).",
